# High Noon's limit counts spells cast, not spells resolved (ruling 2024-04-12: "If you cast a spell that was
# countered, you can't cast another spell during the same turn"). Bot2 casts High Noon on turn 4 (its own Moxen and
# land were cast before it was out). On turn 5 Bot1 casts Ornithopter; Bot2 answers with Lose Focus replicated once
# (CR 702.56a): the original is Bot2's one spell of the turn, and a second spell (Lightning Bolt, with its red mana
# untapped) is refused. The replicated copy is put on the stack, not cast (CR 707.10), so it takes no part in the
# count. Ornithopter is countered, and Bot1's later Mox Jet is still refused because the countered Ornithopter was cast.

[Bot1 Deck]
Ornithopter
Mox Jet
Plains x18

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Mox Pearl
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Sapphire
High Noon
Lose Focus
Lightning Bolt
Island x11

